findings.problem:
Detached build jobs run in the build-jail profile: no user bus, the record root read-only, no steering. From there they are told to:
- stop and restart the live controller, runner, bridge, launcher and worker (the cold-start drill), although the launcher reserves those for drain/release;
- Pause and Emergency-stop `smatsprint-exp.slice`, the slice they run inside (the Integration group), which kills the suite itself;
- start sandbox units (the Lanes group);
- steer the live experiment and confirm a Promote (the M3 acceptance rehearsal), which the build spool and H.8's cgroup rule both refuse;
- run the migration rehearsal's lab hops, which need systemd units.
No part defines a separate test instance (unit names, slices, state root). As written, these suites cannot run, or they would disrupt the live campaign and pollute its ledger.

summary:
40 findings reported (5 blocker, 16 major, 19 minor); 2 more minor ones exist and are omitted: the bare milestone name 'M1' in C.11 ('In M1 measure') and R.5 ('from the M1 measurements'), which should read M1a (Q1); and the README's 'Tap one test button' against N.9 step 7, which needs a tap, a reply and a stale-button press from the user. Scope: the assembled CODEX_MASTER_PROMPT.md is byte-identical to a fresh assembly of parts/, and tools/check_prompt.py finds no unresolved section reference. Line numbers refer to CODEX_MASTER_PROMPT.md unless a quote names 00_README.md or DECISIONS_FOR_APPLYING.md. Main pattern: the five editors made unattended build sessions safe (jail, launcher, no steering), but the milestones still assign those sessions steps that need the forbidden powers:
- pause and resume (the M1a campaign-start gate; R.9's resume after every release, which leaves the campaign PAUSED(by: user));
- opening M1b's gate epoch, which is SSH-only, so the runner refuses to start;
- writing `work/refdata/` and the secrets directory;
- stopping live units (the cold-start drill; the Integration suite pausing its own slice);
- a command-string detach.
A few new launcher named operations plus a separate test instance fix most of them (FC-01, 02, 04, 05, 06, 11, 28). One gate circularity: the 100-episode fall rate versus E = 20 before the first noise floor, which runs only after L1 (FC-03). Sheet deviations: sandbox seed pools (FC-16), learning-parity block count (FC-18), K-env at Stage 4 (FC-19), hardware class (FC-25). Safety: the Vast key bound into M5 Codex sessions (FC-12), `~/.codex` writable by every session (FC-13), and forge-memory admission possibly deferred to M1b (FC-14). Other majors: `smatsprint-build.slice` cannot be top-level under systemd's dash-naming rule, verified against systemd.slice(5) (FC-15); MyoSuite in the science group (FC-17); hashes pinned to L0 (FC-07); the catalogue freeze treating M1b blocks like Promote (FC-08); the public timestamp on gh-pages (FC-09); and the README misquoting L3 as per-seed (FC-21).
